OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGALBANIAN REFUGEES RETURN
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGHOME FROM ITALY
OL,4,    F
OL,5, The Italian authorities have allowed an
OL,6, Albanian ship they impounded at the
OL,7, port of Brindisi to return home.
OL,9,FAbout 2,000 Albanian refugees angry
OL,10,Fabout the squalid conditions at
OL,11,FBrinsidi are on board the ship, Tirana.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FThe Italian authorities are moving many
OL,14,Fthousands of Albanians who have arrived
OL,15,Fat the port to camps set up by the
OL,16,FInternational Red Cross in Sicily. The
OL,17,FEC has also provided emergency aid.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FItaly wants to repatriate the Albanians
OL,20,Fbut has asked the Albanian government
OL,21,Fto guarantee they will not be punished.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG10-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
